{
  "text": "Before you hire your next employee, what if everyone on your team had their own team of AI employees? AI personal assistants, AI video editors, AI web designers, AI market researchers, AI competitive analysts, AI marketing managers. This is exponential time and money being saved while drastically improving team output. Most people use AI like a search tool. Type a question, get a response. Help me write this email. And then manually paste it into Gmail. That's using about 3% of what AI is capable of. What if you could tap into the real superpowers? Agenic workflows where the AI can handle repetitive tasks in the background, learning every time they complete a task. Building one centralized AI brain that increases efficiency and improves output quality across the board. Picture each AI employee with one clear job. One handles your schedule. One edits your videos. One keeps an eye on your competitors. and with a few simple setup files that spell out how you work, each one learns to do things your way. No coding or AI experience required. Now picture a small team of real people, each armed with a team of their own AI employees. Together, they eliminate repetitive, unfulfilling tasks and focus on the work they truly love, solving problems and building real value for the people they serve. The first AI employee takes about 30 minutes to set up. And from there, you build the team one hire at a time. The future of work isn't people or AI. It's people with AI working side by side. And the ones who learn it early will be the ones who get to build what's next.",
